                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Avoid acute illness influence as infections may transiently elevate glucose levels. Document recent steroid or corticosteroid therapy affecting glycemic readings. Ensure proper venipuncture technique to prevent hemolysis interference. Avoid excessive physical exertion before sample collection for stable glucose values. Record patient stress status as it may alter transient blood sugar levels. Ensure correct anticoagulant tube usage for plasma glucose estimation accuracy. Verify patient identity to prevent sample mix-up in metabolic screening panels. Maintain proper sample transport temperature to prevent glycolysis errors. Avoid delayed processing beyond recommended time for glucose stability. Document fasting status clearly if mixed panel interpretation is required.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": null,
                                                    "complexity": null,
                                                    "duration": "",
                                                    "testtype": null,
                                                    "smapletype": "Venous blood",
                                                    "isFasting": "no",
