                                                    "_id": "69cf91688cddfaca6f77f5da",
                                                    "name": "Bone Scan",
                                                    "description": "<p>Bone Scan is a nuclear imaging technique used to evaluate bone metabolism and detect abnormalities in the skeletal system. It involves the use of a small amount of radioactive tracer that accumulates in areas of increased bone activity. The scan helps identify fractures, infections, tumors, and degenerative bone diseases. It is highly sensitive and can detect changes earlier than standard X-rays. The procedure provides a whole-body overview of bone health. It is commonly used in cancer detection and monitoring metastasis. The scan helps diagnose unexplained bone pain. It plays a key role in early detection and treatment planning. The procedure is safe and widely used in clinical practice. It provides valuable diagnostic information for doctors.</p>",
                                                    "subcategory": "69ce898676b5f73f0b0e59c5",
                                                    "brand": null,
                                                    "composition": null,
