                                                    "_id": "69d10cbb844f58462ba42bdf",
                                                    "name": "Growth Scan",
                                                    "description": "<p>Growth Scan is an ultrasound procedure used to assess the growth and development of the fetus during pregnancy. It provides real-time imaging of the baby inside the uterus. The scan helps measure fetal size and weight. It is commonly performed in the second and third trimester. The procedure evaluates fetal organs and overall development. It helps monitor amniotic fluid levels and placenta position. The scan is important for detecting growth abnormalities. It assists in assessing fetal well-being. The procedure is safe and does not involve radiation. It is widely used in routine prenatal care. The imaging results help guide pregnancy management. It plays a key role in ensuring healthy fetal development.</p>",
