                                                        "name": "Ultrasound Scan ",
                                                        "description": "Ultrasound Scan, also known as Sonography, is a non-invasive diagnostic imaging technique that uses high-frequency sound waves to produce real-time images of internal body structures.\nIt is widely used to examine organs such as the liver, kidneys, gallbladder, pancreas, and reproductive organs.\nThe scan is commonly performed in pregnancy to monitor fetal growth and development.\nUltrasound helps detect abnormalities like cysts, tumors, stones, and fluid collections.\nIt allows dynamic assessment of organ movement and blood flow using Doppler technology.\nThe procedure does not involve ionizing radiation, making it safe for repeated use.\nIt is often used as a first-line imaging method due to its accessibility and cost-effectiveness.\nThe scan provides immediate visual feedback, aiding quick clinical decisions.\nIt is useful in guiding procedures such as biopsies and fluid aspiration.\nUltrasound imaging is painless and generally requires minimal preparation.\nThe technique is widely available in hospitals and diagnostic centers.\nIt plays a crucial role in routine and emergency medical evaluations.",
