                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Accurate dating of pregnancy is essential for correct interpretation. Patients should inform about previous pregnancy complications or genetic conditions. A moderately filled bladder may be required depending on scan type. Excess abdominal pressure should be avoided during early pregnancy scans. Movement during scan can affect measurement accuracy and should be minimized. Emotional stress should be reduced to ensure smooth examination. Previous ultrasound reports should be shared for correlation. Patients should understand that this is a screening—not diagnostic—test. Follow-up testing may be required based on results. Proper positioning is required for accurate fetal neck measurement. Timing of scan within the recommended gestational window is critical. Clear communication with the sonographer ensures accurate results.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>NT Scan is completely safe and does not involve radiation. There are no known harmful effects on the fetus. The procedure is non-invasive and painless. Some patients may feel mild pressure from the probe. No post-procedure complications are expected.</p>",
                                                    "complexity": null,
                                                    "duration": null,
                                                    "testtype": null,
                                                    "smapletype": null,
                                                    "isFasting": null,
                                                    "normalrange": null,
