                                                    "bodypart": "Fetus (Neck Region)",
                                                    "iscontrast": "no",
                                                    "procedureType": null,
                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>The patient is positioned comfortably for ultrasound examination. A transabdominal or transvaginal approach may be used based on visibility. Ultrasound gel is applied to improve image transmission. The sonographer locates the fetus and confirms gestational age. Precise measurement of nuchal translucency is performed. Multiple images are captured to ensure accuracy. Fetal position may be adjusted for optimal measurement. Additional anatomical observations are recorded. The scan usually takes about 15 to 20 minutes. Results are calculated based on standardized guidelines. The findings may be combined with blood test results. A report is generated for further clinical interpretation.</p>",
