                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients must disclose any history of diabetes, as blood sugar levels affect tracer uptake. Fasting for several hours is usually required before tracer injection. Recent chemotherapy or radiation therapy should be reported. Physical exertion prior to scan should be avoided to prevent false uptake in muscles. Patients should remain relaxed after tracer injection to ensure accurate distribution. Cold environments should be avoided as they can influence tracer localization. Medications affecting metabolism should be discussed beforehand. Hydration is important to aid tracer clearance post-scan. Pregnancy or breastfeeding status must be clearly communicated. Movement during uptake phase can alter scan interpretation. Any recent infections or inflammation should be disclosed. Strict adherence to pre-scan preparation improves diagnostic accuracy.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>Exposure to a small amount of radioactive tracer is involved. The radiation dose is controlled and considered safe for diagnostic use. Injection site discomfort may occur briefly. Allergic reactions are extremely rare. Tracer naturally decays and is eliminated from the body over time.</p>",
