                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients should inform about any prior kidney surgery or transplant. Hydration is important before and after the scan unless restricted. Urinary symptoms such as pain or difficulty should be disclosed. Recent imaging studies should be shared for comparison. Pregnancy or breastfeeding status must be clearly communicated. Medications affecting kidney function should be discussed beforehand. Patients should be prepared for intravenous tracer injection. Frequent urination during the test may be required. Movement during imaging can affect functional assessment accuracy. Bladder emptying instructions must be followed carefully. Understanding test duration helps in better cooperation. Follow all preparation instructions provided by the medical team.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>A small amount of radioactive tracer is used in the procedure. Radiation exposure is minimal and considered safe. Injection site discomfort may occur briefly. Allergic reactions are extremely rare. Tracer is naturally eliminated through urine over time.</p>",
