                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients should inform about recent fractures, surgeries, or implants. Hydration is recommended before and after tracer administration. Recent nuclear scans should be disclosed to avoid overlap. Pregnancy or breastfeeding must be clearly communicated. Metallic implants do not interfere but should still be reported. Patients should avoid unnecessary physical exertion before the scan. Painful areas should be pointed out for focused imaging. Understanding scan timing helps reduce anxiety during waiting period. Movement during imaging affects resolution and should be minimized. Patients should follow instructions regarding tracer uptake phase. Bladder emptying before imaging improves pelvic image clarity. Proper cooperation ensures accurate lesion localization.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>A small amount of radioactive tracer is administered. Radiation exposure is minimal and within safe limits. Injection site discomfort may occur briefly. Allergic reactions are extremely rare. Tracer is naturally eliminated from the body over time.</p>",
