                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients should avoid caffeine before the test as it affects stress response. History of heart disease or prior interventions must be disclosed. Medications affecting heart rate should be discussed beforehand. Fasting may be required depending on protocol. Comfortable clothing should be worn for stress testing phase. Patients should inform about any chest discomfort or breathlessness. Diabetic patients may need special preparation. Physical exertion before scan should be avoided. Understanding stress procedure helps reduce anxiety. Pregnancy or breastfeeding must be communicated clearly. Follow instructions regarding medication adjustments carefully. Proper preparation ensures accurate perfusion assessment.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>A small amount of radioactive tracer is used. Stress agents may cause temporary symptoms like flushing or dizziness. Mild chest discomfort may occur during stress phase. Injection site discomfort is possible but brief. Symptoms usually resolve shortly after completion.</p>",
