                                                    "procedureType": null,
                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>An intravenous line is established for tracer injection. Baseline imaging may be performed at rest. A stress test is conducted either by exercise or medication. Tracer is injected during peak stress phase. The patient is then positioned under the SPECT camera. The scanner rotates to capture images of the heart. Both stress and rest images are obtained for comparison. The patient must remain still during imaging. Monitoring is done throughout the procedure. The scan duration varies depending on protocol. Images are reconstructed into perfusion maps. A nuclear cardiologist interprets the results.</p>",
