                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients should inform about symptoms like dry mouth or swelling. Recent radiation therapy to head and neck should be disclosed. Medications affecting salivary secretion should be discussed. Food or drink restrictions may be required before the scan. Patients should avoid chewing gum prior to the test. Smoking before scan can alter gland activity and should be avoided. Understanding stimulation phase is important for cooperation. Movement during imaging should be minimized. Pregnancy or breastfeeding must be communicated clearly. Any prior gland surgery should be reported. Patients should be prepared for taste stimulation during scan. Follow all preparation instructions carefully for accurate results.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>A small amount of radioactive tracer is used. Radiation exposure is minimal and safe. Mild injection site discomfort may occur. Allergic reactions are extremely rare. No long-term side effects are expected.</p>",
