                                                    "medicineType": null,
                                                    "units": null,
                                                    "form": null,
                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients should inform about pain severity and duration. History of trauma or injury should be disclosed. Any swelling or lump should be clearly indicated. Loose clothing is recommended for easy access. Movement during scan should be minimized. Sensitivity or tenderness should be communicated. Previous scrotal conditions should be reported. Proper positioning is required for accurate imaging. Follow technician instructions during scan. Avoid unnecessary movement of legs. Prior reports help in comparison. Cooperation ensures better image quality.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">The procedure is completely safe and non-invasive.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">No radiation exposure is involved.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Mild pressure from probe may cause slight discomfort.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">No complications are expected.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent;\">Safe for repeated evaluation.</span></p>",
