                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The patient lies in a supine position.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Support may be provided under the scrotum.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Ultrasound gel is applied to the area.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The probe is moved gently over scrotal sac.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Testes and surrounding structures are examined.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Blood flow is assessed using Doppler.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Images are captured in multiple views.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The scan usually takes 15–20 minutes.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Real-time imaging ensures accurate diagnosis.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The gel is cleaned after the procedure.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">The patient can resume normal activity immediately.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent; color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Findings are reviewed by a radiologist.</span></p>",
