                                                    "_id": "69d13249527dc76674a163c2",
                                                    "name": "Virtual Colonoscopy (CT Colonography)",
                                                    "description": "<p>The patient lies on the CT examination table. A small tube is inserted into the rectum to introduce air. The colon is gently inflated for better visualization. CT images are taken in different positions. The scan captures detailed cross-sectional images. 3D reconstruction is performed for analysis. The patient is asked to hold breath briefly during scanning. The procedure typically takes 10–20 minutes. The tube is removed after imaging. The patient can resume normal activity soon after. Images are processed into virtual views of the colon. A radiologist interprets the findings.</p>",
