                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients must undergo bowel preparation before the procedure. Fasting is usually required prior to the scan. Any history of colon disease or surgery should be disclosed. Patients should inform about abdominal pain or bleeding. Contrast allergy should be reported beforehand. Hydration instructions should be followed carefully. Movement during scanning should be avoided. Pregnancy status must be communicated. Follow dietary restrictions as advised before the scan. Previous colon imaging reports should be provided. Patients should understand air insufflation process. Cooperation ensures accurate imaging results.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>Mild abdominal discomfort due to air insufflation may occur. Temporary bloating sensation is common. Exposure to low-dose radiation is involved. Rarely, contrast-related reactions may occur. Symptoms usually resolve shortly after the procedure.</p>",
