                                                    "_id": "69d13249527dc76674a163c3",
                                                    "name": "Whole Body CT",
                                                    "description": "<p>Whole Body CT is an advanced imaging technique used to evaluate multiple regions of the body in a single session. It provides comprehensive cross-sectional images of internal organs, bones, and soft tissues. The scan is commonly used in trauma cases to detect internal injuries quickly. It plays a role in cancer staging and metastasis detection. The technique allows rapid assessment of critical conditions. It helps identify abnormalities across chest, abdomen, pelvis, and brain. The scan provides high-resolution images for accurate diagnosis. It is widely used in emergency and oncology settings. The method enables early detection of systemic diseases. It offers fast scanning with minimal patient discomfort. The scan is useful for health checkups in selected cases. It is a powerful tool in comprehensive diagnostic evaluation.</p>",
