                                                    "precaution": "<p>Patients should inform about any known medical conditions. Contrast allergy must be disclosed if contrast is used. Kidney function should be evaluated before contrast administration. Fasting may be required depending on protocol. Metal objects should be removed before scanning. Patients should remain still during the scan. Pregnancy status must be clearly communicated. Hydration is recommended before and after contrast studies. Previous imaging reports should be shared. Follow breathing instructions carefully. Inform about any implants or medical devices. Cooperation ensures optimal image quality.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>Exposure to ionizing radiation is involved. Contrast injection may cause a warm sensation. Mild discomfort at injection site may occur. Rare allergic reactions to contrast are possible. Most side effects are temporary and manageable.</p>",
