                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>The patient lies on a motorized CT table. The table moves through the CT scanner. X-ray beams capture cross-sectional images of the body. Contrast may be injected if required. The patient is asked to hold breath at intervals. Multiple body regions are scanned sequentially. The scan is completed within a short duration. Images are reconstructed for detailed analysis. The patient remains still throughout the procedure. The scan typically takes 10–30 minutes. Post-scan instructions are given if contrast is used. A radiologist interprets the results.</p>",
