                                                    "precaution": "<p>* Always place the oxygen concentrator on a stable, flat, and well-ventilated surface. * Keep the device away from open flames, smoking materials, sparks, and flammable substances. * Ensure proper airflow around the concentrator by maintaining sufficient clearance from walls or furniture. * Use the oxygen concentrator only according to the prescribed oxygen flow settings advised by a healthcare professional. * Check the power supply, oxygen tubing, filters, and humidifier bottle regularly for proper functioning. * Do not block air intake or exhaust vents during operation. * Keep the oxygen tubing free from bends, twists, or obstructions to maintain proper oxygen flow. * Use only compatible accessories and medical-grade tubing recommended by the manufacturer. * Clean and replace filters regularly to maintain oxygen purity and device efficiency. * Avoid operating the concentrator in excessively humid, dusty, or poorly ventilated environments. * Keep liquids away from electrical components and control systems to prevent electrical hazards. * Do not move the device roughly or place heavy objects on the concentrator. * Elderly or critically ill patients should use the device under caregiver or medical supervision if necessary. * Do not use the concentrator if unusual noise, overheating, warning alarms, or reduced oxygen output is noticed. * Store the oxygen concentrator in a clean, dry, and safe environment when not in use.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>* Keep the oxygen concentrator away from open flames, smoking materials, sparks, and flammable substances at all times. * Place the device on a stable, flat, and well-ventilated surface during operation. * Do not block air intake or exhaust vents, as proper airflow is essential for safe functioning. * Use the oxygen concentrator only with the prescribed oxygen flow settings recommended by a healthcare professional. * Inspect the power cord, oxygen tubing, filters, humidifier bottle, and accessories regularly for damage or leakage. * Keep oxygen tubing free from bends, twisting, or obstruction to maintain proper oxygen delivery. * Use only compatible medical-grade accessories and replacement parts approved for the device. * Keep liquids away from electrical components and control systems to avoid electrical hazards. * Do not operate the concentrator in wet, dusty, poorly ventilated, or excessively humid environments. * Replace or clean filters regularly to maintain oxygen purity and equipment efficiency. * Do not use the concentrator if warning alarms, overheating, unusual noise, or reduced oxygen output is observed. * Elderly, critically ill, or oxygen-dependent patients should use the device under caregiver or medical supervision if necessary. * Disconnect the power supply before cleaning or performing maintenance procedures. * Do not attempt unauthorized repairs or modifications to the oxygen concentrator. * Store the oxygen concentrator in a clean, dry, and safe environment when not in use.</p>",
                                                    "complexity": null,
