                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Place the oxygen concentrator on a flat, stable, and well-ventilated surface before use. * Connect the power cord securely to a proper electrical outlet. * Attach the oxygen tubing, nasal cannula, or oxygen mask properly to the oxygen outlet. * Fill the humidifier bottle with clean or distilled water if humidification is required. * Switch on the oxygen concentrator using the power control button. * Adjust the oxygen flow rate according to the prescription or healthcare professionals instructions. * Ensure oxygen is flowing properly before applying the nasal cannula or oxygen mask to the patient. * Keep the device running continuously as advised during oxygen therapy sessions. * Monitor the display panel, oxygen flow meter, and warning indicators regularly during operation. * Clean the oxygen tubing, humidifier bottle, and external surfaces regularly to maintain hygiene. * Clean or replace air filters periodically according to manufacturer recommendations. * Switch off the device properly after use and disconnect accessories carefully if required. * Store the oxygen concentrator in a clean, dry, and safe environment when not in use. * Consult healthcare professionals or authorized technicians for proper operation, maintenance, and troubleshooting guidance if necessary.</p>",
