                                                    "_id": "6a05aeda9136efed592911c3",
                                                    "name": "Oxygen Cylinder",
                                                    "description": "<p>The Oxygen Cylinder is a vital medical oxygen supply device designed to store and deliver compressed medical-grade oxygen for patients requiring respiratory support, oxygen therapy, and emergency breathing assistance. Widely used in hospitals, ICUs, ambulances, clinics, emergency care units, nursing homes, rehabilitation centers, and home healthcare environments, the oxygen cylinder plays a critical role in supporting patients with breathing difficulties, low oxygen levels, respiratory disorders, and emergency medical conditions. It provides a reliable and immediate oxygen source during patient treatment, transportation, and critical care situations. Manufactured using high-quality steel, aluminum alloy, or medical-grade metal materials, the oxygen cylinder is engineered for high-pressure oxygen storage, durability, corrosion resistance, and long-lasting performance. The robust cylindrical construction ensures safe oxygen containment while supporting efficient oxygen delivery during medical use. The cylinder is designed according to medical safety standards and is available in multiple sizes and capacities to meet different clinical and home healthcare requirements. The oxygen cylinder is equipped with precision oxygen regulators, flow meters, pressure gauges, humidifier attachments, and valve control systems that help regulate oxygen delivery according to patient needs. Many models also include trolley support systems, portable carrying handles, safety caps, and wheeled stands for convenient transportation and mobility. The oxygen delivery system can be connected to nasal cannulas, oxygen masks, ventilators, or respiratory support devices for continuous oxygen administration during treatment. The oxygen cylinder is highly beneficial for patients suffering from chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), asthma, pneumonia, respiratory infections, oxygen deficiency conditions, trauma injuries, cardiac emergencies, post-surgical recovery, and critical respiratory disorders. It helps improve oxygen saturation levels, breathing comfort, respiratory stability, and emergency patient management in both clinical and home care settings. Portable oxygen cylinders are also commonly used during patient transportation, ambulance services, and emergency medical response situations. Designed for reliability, safety, durability, and effective respiratory support, the oxygen cylinder is an essential component of modern oxygen therapy and emergency healthcare systems. Its dependable oxygen storage capability, efficient delivery mechanisms, and versatile clinical applications make it a preferred choice among hospitals, healthcare professionals, emergency responders, caregivers, and patients. Suitable for both emergency and long-term oxygen therapy use, the oxygen cylinder significantly enhances respiratory care support, treatment efficiency, patient safety, and healthcare preparedness.</p>",
