                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Place the oxygen cylinder in an upright and secure position before use. * Attach the oxygen regulator, flow meter, humidifier bottle, and oxygen tubing securely to the cylinder valve. * Ensure all connections are properly tightened and free from leakage. * Open the cylinder valve slowly and carefully using the appropriate control knob. * Adjust the oxygen flow rate according to the prescription or healthcare professionals instructions. * Connect the nasal cannula, oxygen mask, or respiratory support device properly to the oxygen outlet. * Confirm proper oxygen flow before applying the oxygen delivery device to the patient. * Monitor the pressure gauge regularly to check the remaining oxygen level during use. * Keep the cylinder secured on a trolley, stand, or stable support during operation and transportation. * Close the cylinder valve properly after use to stop oxygen flow completely. * Release any remaining pressure from the regulator after switching off the cylinder. * Clean the regulator, humidifier bottle, tubing, and accessories regularly to maintain hygiene. * Store the oxygen cylinder in a clean, dry, well-ventilated, and safe environment when not in use. * Consult healthcare professionals or authorized technicians for proper operation, refilling, and maintenance guidance if necessary.</p>",
