                                                    "_id": "6a05aeda9136efed592911c9",
                                                    "name": "Patient Monitor",
                                                    "description": "<p>The Patient Monitor is an advanced medical diagnostic and monitoring device designed to continuously track, display, and record vital physiological parameters of patients during medical treatment and critical care management. Widely used in hospitals, ICUs, emergency departments, operation theaters, clinics, ambulances, rehabilitation centers, and healthcare facilities, the patient monitor plays a crucial role in real-time patient assessment, clinical decision-making, and continuous health monitoring. It is specially developed to assist healthcare professionals in monitoring patient condition accurately and responding quickly to any medical changes or emergencies. Manufactured using high-quality medical-grade electronic components and advanced monitoring technology, the patient monitor is engineered for precise data measurement, reliable performance, and long-term clinical operation. The device is designed to monitor multiple vital signs such as heart rate, blood pressure, oxygen saturation (SpO2), respiratory rate, body temperature, electrocardiogram (ECG), pulse rate, and other physiological parameters depending on the model and clinical requirements. The high-resolution digital display provides clear real-time readings and waveform visualization for efficient patient evaluation. The patient monitor is equipped with intelligent alarm systems, touchscreen or digital control panels, data storage capabilities, battery backup systems, and multiple sensor connectivity options for improved patient safety and operational convenience. Many advanced models also include multi-parameter monitoring, wireless connectivity, central monitoring integration, trend analysis, arrhythmia detection, bedside monitoring systems, neonatal or pediatric monitoring modes, and remote patient monitoring compatibility for enhanced critical care management. The patient monitor is highly beneficial for ICU patients, surgical patients, emergency care patients, cardiac patients, neonatal patients, critically ill individuals, and patients requiring continuous medical supervision. It helps healthcare providers detect early physiological changes, improve treatment accuracy, support rapid medical intervention, and enhance patient safety during hospitalization and critical care procedures. Designed for accuracy, reliability, safety, and advanced healthcare monitoring, the patient monitor is an essential component of modern medical diagnostics and patient care systems. Its intelligent monitoring technology, user-friendly interface, real-time data analysis, and dependable performance make it a preferred choice among hospitals, healthcare professionals, emergency care specialists, and critical care units. Suitable for both routine and intensive patient monitoring applications, the patient monitor significantly improves clinical efficiency, patient safety, treatment quality, and overall healthcare management.</p>",
