                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>* Always place the patient monitor on a stable, flat, and dry surface during operation. * Ensure all sensor cables, ECG leads, probes, cuffs, and connectors are properly attached before monitoring. * Use only compatible sensors, accessories, and medical-grade components approved for the monitor model. * Check battery status, power supply connections, and alarm systems regularly before use. * Ensure proper placement of ECG electrodes, SpO2 probes, blood pressure cuffs, and temperature sensors for accurate readings. * Avoid excessive pulling, twisting, or bending of cables and sensor wires during operation. * Keep the monitor away from excessive moisture, liquids, direct heat, or strong electromagnetic interference sources. * Clean and disinfect sensors, cables, probes, and monitor surfaces regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Do not ignore warning alarms, abnormal readings, or error notifications during patient monitoring. * Monitor critically ill patients continuously under qualified healthcare supervision. * Replace damaged cables, probes, sensors, or accessories immediately to maintain accuracy and patient safety. * Avoid placing heavy objects on the monitor or sensor cables. * Disconnect the power supply safely before cleaning or maintenance procedures. * Do not operate the monitor if display malfunctions, unusual noise, overheating, or inaccurate readings are observed. * Store the patient monitor in a clean, dry, and safe healthcare environment when not in use.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>* Always operate the patient monitor on a stable, flat, and dry surface. * Ensure all ECG leads, SpO2 probes, blood pressure cuffs, temperature sensors, and cables are securely connected before monitoring. * Use only compatible medical-grade sensors, accessories, and replacement parts approved for the monitor model. * Verify proper placement of sensors and probes to ensure accurate monitoring results. * Continuously monitor alarms, waveform displays, and vital sign readings during patient observation. * Do not ignore warning alarms, abnormal readings, or system error notifications. * Inspect cables, probes, connectors, batteries, and power cords regularly for damage or wear. * Replace damaged sensors, leads, or accessories immediately to maintain patient safety and monitoring accuracy. * Keep electrical components and monitor surfaces away from water, excessive moisture, or liquid spills. * Avoid excessive pulling, twisting, or bending of monitoring cables during operation. * Critically ill patients should always remain under qualified healthcare supervision while connected to the monitor. * Disconnect the power supply before cleaning, servicing, or maintenance procedures. * Clean and disinfect the monitor, sensors, and cables regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Do not operate the monitor if display malfunction, overheating, unusual noise, or inaccurate readings are observed. * Store the patient monitor in a clean, dry, and safe healthcare environment when not in use.</p>",
