                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Place the patient monitor on a flat, stable, and dry surface before use. * Connect the power supply securely and switch on the monitor. * Attach the required monitoring accessories such as ECG leads, SpO2 probe, blood pressure cuff, temperature sensor, or respiration sensor according to patient requirements. * Ensure all sensors and cables are connected properly to the designated ports on the monitor. * Position the sensors correctly on the patient to obtain accurate vital sign readings. * Configure alarm limits, monitoring parameters, and display settings according to clinical requirements and healthcare guidance. * Monitor the real-time readings, waveforms, and alarm indicators continuously during patient care. * Ensure cables and sensor wires remain untangled and free from obstruction during monitoring. * Respond immediately to warning alarms, abnormal readings, or monitoring errors if observed. * Clean and disinfect the monitor, sensors, probes, and cables regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Replace disposable sensors, ECG electrodes, or damaged accessories periodically according to manufacturer recommendations. * Disconnect the sensors and switch off the monitor properly after use. * Store the patient monitor in a clean, dry, and safe healthcare environment when not in use. * Consult trained healthcare professionals or authorized technical staff for proper setup, troubleshooting, and maintenance guidance if necessary.</p>",
