                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>* Operate the syringe pump only by trained healthcare professionals or qualified caregivers. * Verify the correct medication, syringe size, dosage, and infusion rate before starting therapy. * Use only compatible syringes, IV tubing, and accessories approved for the syringe pump model. * Ensure the syringe is properly loaded and securely locked into the pump before operation. * Remove all air bubbles from the syringe and tubing before connecting to the patient. * Check all tubing connections carefully for leakage, kinks, or blockage before infusion. * Monitor the infusion site regularly for swelling, redness, leakage, or signs of infiltration. * Keep the syringe pump securely mounted on an IV stand or stable surface during operation. * Monitor battery status, alarm systems, and infusion settings regularly throughout therapy. * Respond immediately to occlusion alarms, syringe displacement alerts, low battery warnings, or infusion errors. * Do not operate the device if unusual noise, display malfunction, inaccurate flow, or warning errors are observed. * Clean and disinfect the syringe pump, control panel, and accessories regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Replace damaged syringes, tubing, batteries, or accessories immediately to maintain patient safety and infusion accuracy. * Keep the device away from water, excessive moisture, direct heat, and electromagnetic interference sources. * Disconnect the power supply safely before cleaning or maintenance procedures.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>* Operate the syringe pump only by trained healthcare professionals or qualified caregivers. * Verify the correct medication, syringe size, dosage, infusion rate, and patient information before starting therapy. * Use only compatible syringes, IV tubing, and accessories approved for the syringe pump model. * Ensure the syringe is properly loaded and securely locked into the pump before infusion begins. * Remove all air bubbles from the syringe and infusion tubing to reduce the risk of air embolism. * Inspect tubing connections carefully for leaks, kinks, blockage, or disconnection before and during operation. * Monitor the infusion site regularly for swelling, redness, leakage, or signs of infiltration. * Keep the syringe pump securely mounted on an IV stand or stable support during operation. * Monitor alarms, battery status, infusion flow, and programmed settings continuously throughout therapy. * Respond immediately to occlusion alarms, syringe displacement warnings, low battery alerts, or infusion errors. * Replace damaged syringes, tubing, batteries, or accessories immediately to maintain patient safety and infusion accuracy. * Keep the device away from water, excessive moisture, direct heat, and strong electromagnetic interference sources. * Do not operate the syringe pump if unusual noise, display malfunction, inaccurate flow, or warning errors are observed. * Clean and disinfect the syringe pump, control panel, and accessories regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Disconnect the power supply safely before cleaning, servicing, or maintenance procedures.</p>",
