                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Place the syringe pump securely on an IV stand or stable mounting surface before operation. * Connect the power supply or ensure the battery is sufficiently charged before use. * Switch on the syringe pump using the power control button. * Prepare the prescribed medication and fill the compatible syringe according to clinical requirements. * Remove all air bubbles from the syringe and infusion tubing before setup. * Load the syringe correctly into the syringe pump and secure it according to manufacturer instructions. * Connect the infusion tubing securely to the patients intravenous access point. * Program the required infusion rate, dosage, volume, and delivery parameters according to medical prescriptions. * Confirm all programmed settings carefully before starting the infusion. * Start the infusion and monitor the display screen, flow rate, alarms, and patient condition continuously during therapy. * Respond immediately to occlusion alarms, low battery alerts, syringe displacement warnings, or infusion errors if observed. * Stop the infusion and disconnect the syringe and tubing carefully after completing therapy. * Clean and disinfect the syringe pump, control surfaces, and accessories regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Store the syringe pump in a clean, dry, and safe healthcare environment when not in use.</p>",
