                                                    "_id": "69b93629efa20801905a31c9",
                                                    "name": "Teeth Cleaning",
                                                    "description": "<p>Teeth Cleaning is a preventive dental care procedure performed by dental professionals to maintain oral hygiene and support long-term dental health. The treatment focuses on removing plaque buildup, tartar deposits, surface stains, and harmful bacteria that cannot always be eliminated through regular brushing and flossing alone.</p><p><br></p><p>Professional dental cleaning helps reduce the risk of gum disease, tooth decay, bad breath, and other oral health concerns while promoting cleaner teeth and healthier gums. The procedure is commonly recommended as part of routine dental care and preventive oral health maintenance for patients of different age groups.</p><p><br></p><p>During the treatment, specialized dental instruments and professional cleaning equipment are used to gently clean the teeth and gumline. Ultrasonic scaling devices or manual dental tools may be utilized to remove hardened tartar and plaque deposits from tooth surfaces and difficult-to-reach areas. Polishing may also be performed to smooth the tooth surface and reduce minor surface stains for a cleaner appearance.</p><p><br></p><p>Modern Teeth Cleaning procedures are designed to provide effective oral hygiene maintenance with patient comfort and clinical safety in mind. The treatment may also help dental professionals identify early signs of oral health issues during routine examinations.</p><p><br></p><p>Professional dental cleaning is widely performed in general dental clinics, preventive dental care centers, and oral hygiene practices as part of regular oral health management and preventive dentistry programs.</p>",
