                                                    "name": "Fluoride Treatment",
                                                    "description": "<p>Fluoride Treatment is a preventive dental procedure designed to strengthen tooth enamel, reduce the risk of cavities, and support long-term oral health. The treatment involves the professional application of fluoride-based solutions, gels, foams, or varnishes onto the teeth to help protect against tooth decay and enamel weakening.</p><p><br></p><p>Fluoride is a naturally occurring mineral that plays an important role in maintaining tooth strength by supporting enamel remineralization and improving resistance against acid attacks caused by bacteria, sugary foods, and plaque buildup. Professional fluoride treatments are commonly recommended for children, teenagers, and adults who may be at increased risk of dental cavities, enamel erosion, tooth sensitivity, or weakened enamel.</p><p><br></p><p>The procedure typically begins with a dental examination and oral health evaluation to determine the patient’s preventive dental care needs. After cleaning and drying the teeth if required, the fluoride material is carefully applied to the tooth surfaces using trays, brushes, swabs, or varnish techniques depending on the treatment method selected.</p><p><br></p><p>Professional fluoride treatments are non-invasive, quick, and painless procedures performed in preventive dental care settings. The fluoride material remains on the teeth for a recommended duration to support absorption and enamel strengthening before patients resume normal oral activities according to dentist instructions.</p><p><br></p><p>Modern fluoride treatments are widely used in pediatric dentistry, preventive oral healthcare, school dental programs, and general dental clinics as part of routine cavity prevention and oral hygiene maintenance strategies.</p>",
