                                                    "_id": "69f33065457ddb682c3e38e1",
                                                    "name": "provisional acrylic crown",
                                                    "description": "<p>Provisional acrylic crown is a temporary dental restoration placed over a prepared tooth while the permanent crown is being fabricated. It serves to protect the tooth structure, maintain occlusion, and preserve aesthetics during the interim period. The crown is made from acrylic resin material which is easy to shape and adjust. It prevents sensitivity and bacterial contamination of the prepared tooth. It also helps in maintaining proper gum contour and spacing for final restoration. The provisional crown allows patients to function normally without discomfort. It is commonly used in both anterior and posterior restorations. The procedure is quick and cost-effective. It supports the transition to definitive prosthetic treatment. Provisional acrylic crowns are essential in staged restorative procedures.</p>",
