                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Avoid chewing hard or sticky foods on provisional crown. Maintain good oral hygiene practices. Use caution while flossing to prevent dislodgement. Report any looseness or discomfort immediately. Attend follow-up visits for permanent crown placement. Avoid excessive biting forces. Clean crown gently using soft brush. Maintain balanced diet to reduce stress on restoration. Avoid sticky substances like gum. Proper care ensures temporary restoration stability.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>Temporary crown dislodgement may occur due to weak cementation. Marginal leakage may expose tooth to sensitivity. Fracture of acrylic material may occur under stress. Gum irritation may result from poor contouring. Allergic reaction to acrylic is rare. Occlusal discrepancies may cause discomfort. Wear may occur due to low durability. Improper fit may affect adjacent teeth. Sensitivity may persist in some cases. Risks are low and manageable.</p>",
