                                                    "_id": "69f35de9457ddb682c3e5ec3",
                                                    "name": "implant placement",
                                                    "description": "<p>Implant placement is an advanced dental surgical procedure designed to replace missing teeth by inserting a biocompatible titanium fixture into the alveolar bone, functioning as an artificial tooth root. It serves as a foundation for fixed or removable prosthetic restorations, restoring both esthetics and masticatory function. The procedure relies on the biological process of osseointegration, where the implant fuses with surrounding bone to provide long-term stability. Preoperative planning involves detailed clinical evaluation and imaging to determine ideal implant position and angulation. The implant is strategically placed to optimize load distribution and support prosthetic rehabilitation. Healing phase allows integration of implant with bone before prosthetic loading. Implant-supported restorations offer superior function compared to traditional dentures. The treatment preserves bone structure by preventing resorption associated with tooth loss. Maintenance requires excellent oral hygiene and periodic professional care. This procedure significantly enhances oral health, function, and patient confidence.</p>",
