                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Post-operative care following implant placement includes maintaining meticulous oral hygiene to promote healing and prevent infection. Patients are advised to avoid chewing on the surgical site during the initial healing phase. Application of cold compress helps reduce swelling in the first 24 hours. Prescribed medications including antibiotics and analgesics should be taken as directed. A soft diet is recommended until initial healing is achieved. Smoking and alcohol consumption should be avoided as they impair healing. Gentle rinsing with antiseptic mouthwash may be advised after initial healing period. Regular follow-up visits are essential to monitor implant stability and tissue response. Any unusual pain or swelling should be reported immediately. Long-term maintenance includes professional cleaning and periodic radiographic evaluation.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>Implant placement may be associated with post-operative discomfort including pain, swelling, and minor bleeding at the surgical site. Infection can occur if aseptic protocols are not adequately maintained. Failure of osseointegration may result in implant mobility and necessitate removal. Nerve injury can lead to temporary or permanent paresthesia in adjacent areas. Sinus perforation is a potential complication in posterior maxillary implants. Peri-implantitis may develop due to poor oral hygiene leading to inflammation and bone loss. Delayed healing can occur in patients with systemic conditions such as diabetes. Excessive occlusal loading before integration may compromise implant stability. Mechanical complications such as screw loosening or prosthetic fracture may arise. Careful case selection and adherence to protocols minimize these risks.</p>",
                                                    "complexity": "complex",
                                                    "duration": null,
                                                    "testtype": null,
                                                    "smapletype": null,
                                                    "isFasting": null,
                                                    "normalrange": null,
                                                    "machineType": null,
                                                    "homecareMode": null,
                                                    "diagnostictype": null,
                                                    "bodypart": null,
                                                    "iscontrast": null,
                                                    "procedureType": null,
                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>The procedure begins with comprehensive clinical examination and radiographic imaging to assess bone structure and plan implant placement. Local anesthesia is administered to ensure patient comfort throughout the surgery. A surgical incision is made to expose the alveolar bone and create access for implant placement. Sequential drilling is performed to prepare the osteotomy site with precision. The implant fixture is inserted into the prepared site achieving primary stability. A healing abutment or cover screw is placed depending on surgical protocol. The soft tissue is sutured to facilitate healing over a period of weeks to months. Osseointegration phase allows stable integration of implant with bone. After healing, prosthetic components are attached for final restoration. Occlusal adjustments are made to ensure proper function and comfort.</p>",
