                                                    "_id": "69856559f0fcca21b092e916",
                                                    "name": "Giveglow Intense Hydration for Dry Skin Cream",
                                                    "description": "Giveglow Intense Hydration for Dry Skin Cream is used to treat and prevent dry, rough, scaly, itchy and minor skin irritations like rashes. It works by forming an oily layer over the skin, thus helps to retain moisture and prevents flaking. It may also be used as a laxative to treat constipation. Giveglow Intense Hydration for Dry Skin Cream should be used in the dose and duration as advised by your doctor. There are no common side effects seen with this medicine. However, slight burning sensation, irritation or redness may occur sometimes. Please consult your doctor if these do not resolve or bother you.Before taking Giveglow Intense Hydration for Dry Skin Cream, you should tell your doctor if you have diabetes or if you are unable to digest milk sugar (lactose intolerant). If you use this medicine over a long period of time, your doctor may want you to have occasional blood tests to check the mineral levels (e.g. potassium and sodium). Do not take other laxative medicines while taking this medicine and check with your doctor if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.\n\n              How to Use:\n              This medicine is for external use only. Use it in the dose and duration as advised by your doctor. Check the label for directions before use. Clean and dry the affected area and apply the cream. Wash your hands after applying, unless hands are the affected area.\n\n              Safety Advice:\n              - Alcohol : None <p> No interaction found/established | - Pregnancy : CONSULT YOUR DOCTOR <p> Giveglow Intense Hydration for Dry Skin Cream may be unsafe to use during pregnancy. Although there are limited studies in humans, animal studies have shown harm\n\n              If Missed:\n              If you miss a dose of Giveglow Intense Hydration for Dry Skin Cream, skip it and continue with your normal schedule. Do not double the dose.\\\\n",
