                                                    "name": "Post-Surgery Physiotherapy at Home",
                                                    "description": "<h4>Post-Surgery Physiotherapy at Home is a specialized rehabilitation and recovery service designed to help patients regain mobility, strength, flexibility, and physical independence after surgical procedures within the comfort of their home environment. Surgery can lead to pain, stiffness, muscle weakness, swelling, reduced movement, and difficulty performing daily activities. Professional physiotherapy support plays an important role in accelerating recovery, preventing complications, improving physical function, and supporting safe healing after surgery.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>This service is especially beneficial for patients recovering from orthopedic surgeries, joint replacement procedures, spinal surgeries, fracture surgeries, neurological surgeries, abdominal surgeries, sports injury surgeries, ligament repair procedures, cardiac surgeries, and other major or minor surgical interventions. Elderly patients and individuals with mobility limitations can also benefit from continuous physiotherapy and rehabilitation support at home.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Trained physiotherapists and rehabilitation professionals provide personalized treatment plans according to the patient’s surgical condition, mobility level, pain severity, physical limitations, recovery goals, and doctor’s recommendations. The therapy program may include stretching exercises, muscle strengthening, balance training, posture correction, walking assistance, breathing exercises, joint mobility exercises, pain management techniques, gait training, flexibility improvement exercises, and recovery-focused rehabilitation support.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Post-Surgery Physiotherapy at Home also includes continuous monitoring for pain, swelling, stiffness, weakness, balance problems, fatigue, breathing discomfort, wound-related movement limitations, or rehabilitation-related complications. Early identification of concerns helps ensure safer recovery and improved rehabilitation outcomes.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Healthcare professionals educate patients and caregivers regarding safe movement techniques, posture support, fall prevention, walking aid usage, breathing exercises, home exercise routines, rehabilitation precautions, pain management strategies, and long-term physical wellness practices. Emotional encouragement and compassionate support also help improve confidence and motivation during the recovery process.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Receiving Post-Surgery Physiotherapy at Home allows patients to continue rehabilitation comfortably within a familiar and emotionally supportive environment while reducing travel-related strain and repeated hospital visits. The service promotes faster healing, improved mobility, reduced pain and stiffness, enhanced strength and flexibility, increased physical independence, safer recovery support, and continuous professional physiotherapy care at home.</h4>",
