                                                    "_id": "69a13dd8a60e62715b176742",
                                                    "name": "FlexCare Home Physio",
                                                    "description": "<h4>FlexCare Home Physio is a specialized home physiotherapy and rehabilitation service designed to provide professional physical therapy, mobility support, pain management, and recovery care within the comfort of the patient’s home environment. This service focuses on improving movement, flexibility, strength, balance, posture, and overall physical function for individuals recovering from injuries, surgeries, neurological conditions, orthopedic disorders, or mobility limitations.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>FlexCare Home Physio is especially beneficial for elderly individuals, post-surgical patients, stroke recovery patients, orthopedic rehabilitation patients, sports injury patients, paralysis patients, individuals with chronic pain, arthritis, back pain, neck pain, joint stiffness, and patients requiring long-term physiotherapy and mobility support. Personalized physiotherapy care helps patients recover safely while reducing the need for repeated hospital or clinic visits.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Trained physiotherapists and rehabilitation professionals provide customized treatment plans according to the patient’s medical condition, mobility level, pain severity, physical limitations, rehabilitation goals, and doctor’s recommendations. The service may include stretching exercises, muscle strengthening, mobility training, posture correction, balance improvement, gait training, joint movement exercises, pain management therapy, respiratory physiotherapy, neurological rehabilitation, and recovery-focused physical therapy support.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>FlexCare Home Physio also includes continuous monitoring for pain, swelling, stiffness, weakness, balance issues, reduced movement, muscle tightness, fatigue, or rehabilitation-related complications. Early identification of concerns helps ensure safer recovery and improved rehabilitation outcomes.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Healthcare professionals guide patients and caregivers regarding safe movement techniques, home exercise routines, posture management, fall prevention, mobility aids, rehabilitation precautions, breathing exercises, and long-term physical wellness practices. Emotional encouragement and compassionate support help improve patient confidence and motivation during rehabilitation.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Receiving FlexCare Home Physio allows patients to continue physiotherapy and recovery comfortably in a familiar environment while reducing physical strain, travel inconvenience, and stress associated with hospital visits. The service promotes faster recovery, improved mobility, pain relief, better flexibility, enhanced independence, safer rehabilitation support, and continuous professional physiotherapy care at home.</h4>",
