                                                    "_id": "69a14492a60e62715b177161",
                                                    "name": "Continuous Oxygen Therapy",
                                                    "description": "<h4>Continuous Oxygen Therapy is a specialized respiratory healthcare service designed to provide uninterrupted oxygen support for patients who require long-term or continuous oxygen supplementation due to respiratory or medical conditions affecting normal breathing and oxygen levels. This therapy helps maintain adequate oxygen saturation, improve breathing comfort, reduce respiratory distress, and support overall body function and recovery.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>This service is especially beneficial for patients with chronic respiratory diseases, COPD (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease), asthma, pneumonia recovery, pulmonary fibrosis, post-COVID respiratory complications, heart failure, sleep-related breathing disorders, neurological conditions, bedridden patients, and individuals requiring long-term oxygen support. Elderly patients and post-ICU recovery patients can also benefit from continuous respiratory monitoring and oxygen management at home.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Trained respiratory therapists, nurses, and healthcare professionals provide personalized oxygen therapy support according to the patient’s respiratory condition, oxygen saturation levels, breathing patterns, medical history, and doctor’s recommendations. The service may include oxygen concentrator setup, oxygen cylinder management, nasal cannula or mask support, oxygen flow monitoring, respiratory assessment, vital signs monitoring, airway support, breathing comfort supervision, and emergency respiratory care assistance.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Continuous Oxygen Therapy also includes monitoring for low oxygen levels, breathing difficulty, chest discomfort, oxygen equipment malfunction, dryness, respiratory infections, fatigue, or signs of respiratory distress. Continuous observation helps ensure safer oxygen delivery and timely medical intervention if complications arise.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Healthcare professionals maintain strict hygiene and safety standards while handling oxygen equipment and respiratory accessories. Patients and caregivers also receive guidance regarding oxygen device usage, equipment maintenance, respiratory hygiene, fire safety precautions, emergency response measures, and recognizing warning signs that may require immediate medical attention.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Receiving Continuous Oxygen Therapy at home allows patients to continue respiratory treatment in a familiar and comfortable environment while reducing unnecessary hospital stays and improving emotional well-being. The service promotes stable oxygen support, improved breathing comfort, enhanced recovery management, reduced respiratory strain, better quality of life, and continuous professional respiratory healthcare supervision at home.</h4>",
