                                                    "_id": "69a16ba6a60e62715b177f94",
                                                    "name": "Postnatal Care at Home",
                                                    "description": "<h4>Postnatal Care at Home is a specialized maternal healthcare service designed to provide professional medical care, recovery support, emotional guidance, and wellness monitoring for mothers after childbirth within the comfort and safety of their home environment. The postnatal period is an important phase where mothers require proper care to recover physically, emotionally, and mentally after delivery while adapting to newborn care responsibilities.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>This service is especially beneficial for mothers recovering after normal delivery, cesarean section (C-section), complicated childbirth, multiple births, or high-risk pregnancies. First-time mothers, mothers experiencing weakness, breastfeeding difficulties, pain, or post-delivery stress can also benefit from continuous professional support and healthcare supervision.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Trained nurses, caregivers, and maternal healthcare professionals provide personalized care according to the mother’s health condition, delivery type, recovery progress, nutritional requirements, medications, and doctor’s recommendations. The service may include vital signs monitoring, wound care, pain management observation, breastfeeding support, hygiene assistance, medication reminders, hydration monitoring, mobility assistance, emotional care, nutritional guidance, and postnatal wellness supervision.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Postnatal Care at Home also includes monitoring for symptoms such as fever, excessive bleeding, swelling, infection signs, weakness, breastfeeding difficulties, dehydration, pain, mood changes, or postpartum complications. Continuous monitoring helps identify health concerns early and supports safer maternal recovery and timely medical intervention when required.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Healthcare professionals educate mothers and caregivers regarding postnatal hygiene, breastfeeding techniques, healthy nutrition, newborn care basics, safe physical activity, medication schedules, emotional wellness, and recovery precautions. Emotional reassurance and compassionate guidance help reduce postpartum stress and improve confidence during motherhood.</h4><h4><br></h4><h4>Receiving Postnatal Care at Home allows mothers to recover comfortably in a familiar and emotionally supportive environment while reducing unnecessary hospital visits and physical strain. The service promotes faster healing, improved maternal health, better breastfeeding support, enhanced comfort, reduced stress, healthier recovery, and continuous professional healthcare supervision after childbirth.</h4>",
