                                                    "_id": "69a1746945179c41f2b1cf37",
                                                    "name": "Colic & Digestive Support",
                                                    "description": "<p>Colic &amp; Digestive Support is a specialized pediatric home healthcare service designed to help infants and young babies experiencing colic symptoms, digestive discomfort, gas problems, feeding-related issues, and stomach discomfort. Digestive issues are common during the early months of life and may lead to excessive crying, irritability, poor sleep, feeding difficulties, bloating, constipation, or discomfort after feeding. Proper digestive support and professional guidance help improve baby comfort, feeding routines, and overall well-being.</p><p><br></p><p>This service is especially beneficial for newborns, infants with colic symptoms, premature babies, babies experiencing gas discomfort, reflux, constipation, indigestion, feeding intolerance, bloating, excessive crying, or irregular bowel movements. Professional digestive care support helps parents manage these concerns safely and effectively within the comfort of home.</p><p><br></p><p>Trained pediatric caregivers, nurses, and healthcare professionals provide personalized support according to the baby’s age, feeding habits, digestive condition, sleep patterns, medical history, and pediatric recommendations. The service may include feeding guidance, burping support, tummy comfort techniques, bottle-feeding assistance, breastfeeding support, hydration monitoring, sleep routine guidance, baby massage techniques, and observation of digestive patterns.</p><p><br></p><p>Colic &amp; Digestive Support also includes monitoring for vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, excessive gas, abdominal discomfort, feeding difficulties, dehydration, poor sleep, unusual crying patterns, reflux symptoms, or signs of infection. Early identification of digestive concerns helps ensure timely pediatric consultation and safer infant care management.</p><p><br></p><p>Healthcare professionals educate parents and caregivers regarding proper feeding positions, burping techniques, safe formula preparation, breastfeeding practices, tummy care, hydration support, digestive comfort methods, sleep positioning, and recognizing warning signs that may require medical attention. Emotional reassurance and compassionate guidance also help reduce stress for parents during infant care.</p><p><br></p><p>Receiving Colic &amp; Digestive Support at home allows babies to receive continuous digestive care and comfort support within a familiar and soothing environment while reducing unnecessary clinic visits and parental anxiety. The service promotes better digestion, improved feeding comfort, reduced colic symptoms, healthier sleep routines, enhanced baby comfort, and continuous professional pediatric healthcare support.</p>",
