                                                    "strength": null,
                                                    "directionofuse": null,
                                                    "precaution": "<p>* Always adjust the walker height properly according to the users height before use. * Ensure all wheels, locks, joints, and folding mechanisms are securely fixed before walking. * Check the wheels and anti-slip rubber tips regularly for wear or damage. * Use the walker only on stable, flat, and dry surfaces for better safety. * Avoid using the walker on wet, slippery, oily, or uneven floors without assistance. * Do not exceed the recommended weight capacity of the walker. * Hold both hand grips firmly while walking to maintain balance and control. * Move the walker slowly and carefully to avoid sudden imbalance or falls. * Use wheel locks properly if the walker is equipped with locking mechanisms. * Elderly or physically weak users should use the walker under supervision during initial use if necessary. * Inspect the frame, screws, wheels, and support structures regularly for looseness or damage. * Do not use the walker if it becomes unstable, bent, cracked, or structurally damaged. * Foldable models should be locked securely before use to prevent accidental collapse. * Clean the walker regularly using a soft cloth and mild disinfectant to maintain hygiene and durability. * Store the walker in a clean and dry place away from excessive moisture or corrosive substances.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>* Use the walker only after proper height adjustment and secure locking of all components. * Ensure the wheels, brakes, and anti-slip rubber tips are in good condition before every use. * Do not use the walker on wet, slippery, oily, or uneven surfaces without assistance. * Always hold both hand grips firmly while walking. * Move the walker slowly and carefully to maintain balance and prevent falls. * Apply wheel locks when standing still if the walker includes braking mechanisms. * Do not exceed the recommended weight capacity of the walker. * Inspect the frame, screws, joints, wheels, and locking systems regularly for looseness or damage. * Replace worn-out wheels, rubber tips, or damaged components immediately. * Foldable models must be fully locked before use to prevent accidental collapse. * Elderly or physically weak users should use the walker under caregiver supervision if necessary. * Avoid sudden turning, excessive leaning, or rapid movement while using the walker. * Keep the walking area free from obstacles, water, or loose objects to reduce fall risk. * Clean and dry the walker regularly to maintain hygiene and durability. * Do not use the walker if it becomes unstable, bent, cracked, or structurally damaged.</p>",
