                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Adjust the walker height according to the user�s comfort and proper walking posture before use. * Ensure all wheels, locks, joints, and folding mechanisms are securely fixed. * Place the walker firmly on the ground and maintain a balanced standing position. * Hold both hand grips evenly and firmly for better balance and support. * Push the walker gently forward using the wheels without lifting it completely unless required. * Walk slowly and carefully while maintaining proper posture and balance. * Use the walker only on flat, stable, and dry surfaces for safer mobility. * Apply wheel locks when standing still if the walker is equipped with locking brakes. * Avoid sudden turns, rapid movement, or excessive leaning during use. * Check the wheels and anti-slip rubber tips regularly for smooth movement and stability. * Fold the walker carefully after use if using a foldable model for easy storage or transport. * Clean the walker frame, wheels, and hand grips regularly using a soft cloth and mild disinfectant. * Inspect the frame, screws, wheels, and locking mechanisms periodically for wear or damage. * Store the walker in a clean, dry, and safe place when not in use.</p>",
