                                                    "procedureType": null,
                                                    "recoveryTime": null,
                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Place the wheelchair stretcher on a flat, stable, and dry surface before use. * Engage all wheel locks or brakes before transferring the patient. * Assist the patient carefully while sitting or lying on the wheelchair stretcher. * Ensure the patient is properly positioned and supported before movement. * Adjust the backrest, stretcher position, or reclining angle gently according to patient comfort and medical requirements. * Secure side rails, safety belts, footrests, and armrests properly before transportation. * Release the wheel locks only when ready to move the wheelchair stretcher. * Push the stretcher slowly and carefully while maintaining full control and balance. * Move cautiously on ramps, uneven floors, elevators, or crowded hospital areas. * Apply brakes immediately whenever the wheelchair stretcher is stationary. * Use proper transfer techniques while converting between wheelchair and stretcher modes. * Inspect the wheels, brakes, frame, mattress, and adjustment mechanisms regularly for proper functioning. * Clean and disinfect the mattress, frame, side rails, and support surfaces after every use to maintain hygiene. * Store the wheelchair stretcher in a clean, dry, and safe location when not in use.</p>",
