                                                    "precaution": "<p>* Use the BiPAP machine only according to the prescribed settings advised by a healthcare professional. * Always place the device on a stable, flat, and well-ventilated surface during operation. * Ensure the mask, tubing, humidifier, and filters are properly connected before use. * Check the mask fit carefully to prevent excessive air leakage and maintain effective therapy. * Keep the air intake and ventilation openings free from blockage during operation. * Use only compatible masks, tubing, filters, and accessories recommended for the BiPAP machine model. * Clean and disinfect the mask, tubing, humidifier chamber, and filters regularly to maintain hygiene and infection control. * Replace filters, tubing, and masks periodically according to manufacturer recommendations. * Keep liquids away from electrical components and power connections to avoid electrical hazards. * Do not use the machine if unusual noise, warning alarms, overheating, airflow problems, or display errors are noticed. * Ensure proper humidifier water levels if using a heated humidification system. * Avoid twisting, bending, or blocking the breathing tubing during operation. * Elderly, critically ill, or respiratory-dependent patients should use the device under caregiver or medical supervision if necessary. * Disconnect the power supply before cleaning or maintenance procedures. * Store the BiPAP machine in a clean, dry, and safe environment when not in use.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>* Use the BiPAP machine only with prescribed settings recommended by a qualified healthcare professional. * Always place the device on a stable, flat, and well-ventilated surface during operation. * Ensure the mask, tubing, humidifier chamber, filters, and power connections are securely attached before use. * Keep air intake vents and airflow passages free from blockage to maintain proper ventilation. * Inspect the mask, tubing, filters, humidifier, and power cord regularly for leakage, damage, or wear. * Replace damaged masks, filters, tubing, or accessories immediately to maintain safe and effective therapy. * Keep electrical components and power connections away from water or excessive moisture to prevent electrical hazards. * Use only compatible masks, tubing, filters, and accessories approved for the BiPAP machine model. * Ensure the mask fits properly to reduce excessive air leakage during therapy. * Maintain proper humidifier water levels if using heated humidification support. * Do not operate the machine if warning alarms, unusual noise, overheating, airflow problems, or display errors are observed. * Elderly, critically ill, or respiratory-dependent patients should use the BiPAP machine under caregiver or medical supervision if necessary. * Disconnect the power supply before cleaning, servicing, or maintenance procedures. * Do not attempt unauthorized repairs or modifications to the BiPAP machine. * Store the device in a clean, dry, and safe environment when not in use.</p>",
