                                                    "preparationInstructions": "<p>* Place the BiPAP machine on a flat, stable, and well-ventilated surface before use. * Connect the power supply securely and ensure the device is properly assembled. * Attach the breathing tubing, mask, humidifier chamber, and filters according to the setup instructions. * Fill the humidifier chamber with clean or distilled water if humidification is required. * Wear the mask properly over the nose or nose and mouth to ensure a comfortable and secure fit. * Switch on the BiPAP machine using the power control button. * Adjust the prescribed pressure settings only according to healthcare professional instructions. * Breathe normally while the machine delivers supportive airflow during inhalation and exhalation. * Monitor the display panel, airflow settings, humidifier levels, and warning indicators regularly during use. * Ensure the tubing remains free from twists, bends, or obstruction during therapy. * Clean the mask, tubing, humidifier chamber, and external surfaces regularly to maintain hygiene. * Replace filters, tubing, and accessories periodically according to manufacturer recommendations. * Switch off the machine properly after use and disconnect accessories carefully if required. * Store the BiPAP machine in a clean, dry, and safe environment when not in use.</p>",
