                                                    "_id": "699e98c893e1d97389046e93",
                                                    "name": "Total Artificial Heart Implantation",
                                                    "description": "<p>Total Artificial Heart Implantation is an advanced cardiac surgical procedure in which a mechanical artificial heart device completely replaces the damaged natural heart ventricles. This procedure is mainly performed in patients with severe end-stage heart failure affecting both sides of the heart when other treatments are no longer effective. The artificial heart helps maintain blood circulation and oxygen supply throughout the body until a suitable donor heart becomes available for transplantation or as long-term supportive therapy in selected patients. During the surgery, the diseased ventricles are removed while portions of the upper heart chambers are preserved. The mechanical heart device is then connected to the major blood vessels and attached to an external power source or control system. The procedure is performed under general anesthesia using a heart-lung bypass machine. Total Artificial Heart Implantation can significantly improve survival, organ function, blood circulation, and quality of life in critically ill patients with advanced heart disease. Patients require intensive monitoring after surgery and lifelong medical follow-up to manage device function and prevent complications. Rehabilitation, medication management, infection prevention, and routine device evaluations are important parts of long-term care after implantation</p>",
                                                    "subcategory": "6986f26171d1b4078acc4d94",
                                                    "brand": null,
