                                                    "directionofuse": "<p>Pre Care</p><p>Complete detailed cardiac and overall health evaluation</p><p>Follow all fasting and medication instructions before surgery</p><p>Discuss surgical risks and expectations with the cardiac surgeon</p><p>Prepare for ICU stay and long-term rehabilitation</p><p>Arrange caregiver support for postoperative recovery</p><p>Stop smoking and maintain a healthy diet before surgery</p><p>Post Care</p><p>Monitor device function and vital signs regularly</p><p>Take anticoagulants and prescribed medications exactly as directed</p><p>Maintain cleanliness around external device connections</p><p>Attend frequent follow-up visits and device assessments</p><p>Watch for signs of infection, bleeding, or breathing difficulty</p><p>Follow cardiac rehabilitation and physical therapy plans</p><p>Avoid strenuous physical activities until medically cleared</p><p>Maintain proper nutrition and hydration for recovery</p><p>Learn emergency procedures related to device malfunction or alarms</p>",
                                                    "precaution": "<p>Complete all cardiac evaluations and imaging tests before surgery</p><p>Inform the medical team about allergies, medications, and previous surgeries</p><p>Follow fasting instructions before the operation</p><p>Avoid smoking and alcohol before surgery</p><p>Maintain proper nutrition and hydration</p><p>Follow all anticoagulant and medication guidelines strictly</p><p>Monitor for symptoms such as chest pain, breathlessness, or dizziness</p><p>Maintain sterile handling of external device components</p><p>Attend all scheduled follow-up appointments regularly</p><p>Learn proper handling and maintenance of the artificial heart system</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>Bleeding during or after surgery</p><p>Infection around the device or surgical site</p><p>Blood clot formation and stroke risk</p><p>Device malfunction or mechanical failure</p><p>Irregular heart rhythm complications</p><p>Kidney or liver dysfunction</p><p>Breathing difficulties after surgery</p><p>Reaction to anesthesia</p><p>Fluid accumulation around the lungs or heart</p><p>Need for emergency replacement procedures</p><p>Fatigue and weakness during recovery</p><p>Risk of long-term hospitalization and intensive monitoring</p>",
