                                                    "directionofuse": "<h4>* Undergo complete medical evaluation including physical examination, imaging scans, blood tests, and anesthesia assessment before surgery.</h4><h4>* Inform the healthcare team about all medications, allergies, previous surgeries, bleeding disorders, chronic cough, constipation, and existing medical conditions.</h4><h4>* Follow all fasting instructions carefully before anesthesia and surgery.</h4><h4>* Avoid smoking, alcohol, blood-thinning medications, and certain supplements before surgery as advised by the healthcare provider.</h4><h4>* Maintain proper hydration, balanced nutrition, and infection prevention measures under medical supervision before the procedure.</h4><h4>* Arrange transportation and caregiver support before hospital discharge.</h4><h4>* Follow all hospital hygiene and sterile care protocols carefully before and after surgery.</h4><h4>* After surgery, avoid heavy lifting, strenuous exercise, abdominal strain, coughing pressure, or sudden movements during the healing period.</h4><h4>* Use abdominal support garments or hernia belts only if prescribed by the surgeon.</h4><h4>* Keep surgical wounds clean, dry, and protected throughout the recovery period.</h4><h4>* Take prescribed pain medications, antibiotics, anti-inflammatory medicines, and post-operative treatments exactly as directed.</h4><h4>* Follow dietary instructions carefully, including proper hydration and fiber-rich nutrition to prevent constipation and abdominal pressure.</h4><h4>* Walk gently and perform light movements as advised to improve circulation and reduce the risk of blood clots.</h4><h4>* Monitor for fever, severe pain, swelling, redness, vomiting, wound discharge, breathing difficulty, recurrence of bulging, or signs of infection and report them immediately to healthcare professionals.</h4><h4>* Attend all follow-up appointments for wound assessment, mesh evaluation if used, and recovery monitoring.</h4><h4>* Follow activity restrictions carefully until complete recovery and medical clearance are achieved.</h4><h4><br></h4>",
