                                                    "directionofuse": "<p>* Undergo complete urological evaluation including urine tests, blood tests, ultrasound, CT scan, X-ray, and kidney function assessment before the procedure.</p><p>* Inform the healthcare team about all medications, allergies, bleeding disorders, previous urinary surgeries, and existing medical conditions.</p><p>* Avoid smoking, alcohol, blood-thinning medications, and certain supplements before surgery as advised by the healthcare provider.</p><p>* Follow fasting instructions carefully before anesthesia and surgery.</p><p>* Inform healthcare professionals about fever, urinary infection symptoms, severe pain, or reduced urine output before the procedure.</p><p>* Arrange transportation and caregiver support before hospital discharge.</p><p>* Follow all hospital hygiene and infection prevention guidelines carefully before surgery.</p><p>* After surgery, drink adequate fluids if medically advised to help flush the urinary system and support recovery.</p><p>* Avoid heavy lifting, strenuous exercise, and physically demanding activities during the recovery period.</p><p>* Take prescribed antibiotics, pain medications, urinary medicines, and other post-operative treatments exactly as directed.</p><p>* Follow dietary recommendations carefully to reduce the risk of future kidney stone formation.</p><p>* Monitor for fever, severe pain, difficulty urinating, heavy bleeding in urine, nausea, swelling, or signs of infection and report them immediately to healthcare professionals.</p><p>* Follow instructions carefully if a urinary catheter or ureteral stent has been placed after surgery.</p><p>* Maintain proper hydration, balanced nutrition, and adequate rest to support healing and kidney recovery.</p><p>* Attend all follow-up appointments for stent removal, imaging evaluation, kidney monitoring, and stone analysis if required.</p><p>* Gradually return to normal activities only after medical clearance from the urologist.</p><p>* Maintain long-term kidney health management, hydration habits, and preventive lifestyle changes under medical supervision.</p>",
                                                    "precaution": "<p>* Undergo complete urological evaluation including urine tests, blood tests, ultrasound, CT scan, X-ray, and kidney function assessment before the procedure.</p><p>* Inform the urologist about all medications, allergies, bleeding disorders, previous urinary surgeries, and existing medical conditions before treatment.</p><p>* Avoid smoking, alcohol, blood-thinning medications, and certain supplements before surgery as advised by the healthcare provider.</p><p>* Follow fasting instructions carefully before anesthesia and surgery.</p><p>* Inform healthcare professionals about fever, urinary infection symptoms, severe pain, or reduced urine output before the procedure.</p><p>* Follow all hospital hygiene and infection prevention guidelines carefully before surgery.</p><p>* After surgery, drink adequate fluids if medically advised to help flush the urinary system and support recovery.</p><p>* Avoid heavy lifting, strenuous exercise, and physically demanding activities during the recovery period.</p><p>* Take prescribed antibiotics, pain medications, urinary medicines, and other post-operative treatments exactly as directed.</p><p>* Monitor for fever, severe pain, difficulty urinating, heavy bleeding in urine, nausea, swelling, or signs of infection and report them immediately to healthcare professionals.</p><p>* Follow dietary recommendations carefully to reduce the risk of future kidney stone formation.</p><p>* Avoid dehydration and maintain proper hydration regularly after recovery.</p><p>* Attend all follow-up appointments for stent removal, imaging evaluation, kidney monitoring, and stone analysis if required.</p><p>* Follow instructions carefully if a urinary catheter or ureteral stent has been placed after surgery.</p><p>* Maintain long-term kidney health management and preventive lifestyle changes under medical supervision.</p>",
                                                    "sideeffects": "<p>* Pain, soreness, or discomfort around the surgical area or urinary tract after the procedure.</p><p>* Burning sensation or mild pain during urination during early recovery.</p><p>* Temporary blood in urine (hematuria) after stone removal or laser treatment.</p><p>* Frequent urination, urgency, or urinary discomfort during healing.</p><p>* Mild swelling, fatigue, weakness, or body discomfort after surgery.</p><p>* Nausea, dizziness, or anesthesia-related side effects after the procedure.</p><p>* Temporary difficulty passing urine or bladder irritation in some patients.</p><p>* Mild abdominal, flank, or lower back pain during recovery.</p><p>* Discomfort caused by temporary ureteral stents or urinary catheters if placed after surgery.</p><p>* Passage of small stone fragments or debris in urine after lithotripsy procedures.</p><p>* Risk of urinary tract infection, fever, or inflammation after surgery.</p><p>* Rare complications such as bleeding, kidney injury, ureteral damage, or urinary blockage.</p><p>* Possibility of residual stone fragments requiring additional treatment in some cases.</p><p>* Dehydration or temporary kidney function changes during recovery if fluid intake is inadequate.</p><p>* Risk of kidney stone recurrence if preventive lifestyle and dietary measures are not followed long term.</p>",
